{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7YW5EjvXpsX3PC9jyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job did run every night. It failed twice over, and the first failure stopped the script from reporting the second.\n\n**Causes**\n\n1. **`status=$?` killed the script (the reason for silence).** In `bin/nightly-review.zsh`, zsh treats `status` as read-only. The assignment aborted the script before the failure notification ran. I reproduced this with zsh 5.9. The fix is `rc=$?`, and the failure path now logs and notifies first.\n2. **`Not logged in` (the real failure).** Every run in `nightly-review.err` fails with this. The plist sets only `PATH`, and the CLI looks up its keychain login by user name. I added `USER` to the plist. This is inferred from the error text and the plist. I could not reproduce it under a live launchd.\n\nEvidence the job ran: `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, which matches the six failure blocks in the error log.\n\n**Changes**\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: `rc=$?`, a `fail` helper, `< /dev/null` on the `claude` call, empty output treated as failure, a per-run line with duration in `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.log`, and notifier failures reported and made to exit nonzero.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: `USER` set to `vk`. The paths in the snapshot use `/Users/vk`, so I used that name. Run `id -un` and change it if your short name differs.\n- `ANSWER.md`: causes, evidence, testing, and the colleague-note breakdown.\n\n**Colleague's note.** The `status` point, the `launchctl print` check, `< /dev/null`, `USER`, the duration log and the failure-path ordering all applied. The stdin switch did not: their failure was \"Input must be provided\", which is not in our log, so I kept the prompt as an argument.\n\n**Testing.** I ran the script in a temporary sandbox with stub `claude` and `notify.sh`, under `env -i`. All five cases behaved as intended: claude failure, success, empty output, notifier failure, and missing repo. I deleted the sandbox afterwards. The plist passes `plutil -lint`. I did not run launchd, send a real Telegram message, or commit anything.\n\n**Still for you to do** (the commands are in `ANSWER.md`): copy the files into your home dir, then `bootout` and `bootstrap` the job. `kickstart` alone does not re-read the plist. Then confirm `last exit code = 0`, a fresh non-empty output file, a log line with a plausible duration, and the Telegram message. If `Not logged in` still appears, the keychain login is not reachable from launchd, and that is the next thing to check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":42272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e89afe5e-3ef0-4483-aa0f-cb7291e867d3","uuid":"05d4d3ae-e555-4712-aa24-351418889191","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:30:38.533Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7YVortk2cVYUrH9AwY"}
